Open-core note:
Sofuu follows an open-core model. The MIT License above covers the entire
Sofuu execution runtime codebase: the engine, CLI, JavaScript/TypeScript
APIs, agents, MCP client/server, HTTP, vector operations, local memory,
embeddings, and core developer tooling.

It DOES NOT cover the design, mathematics, or specification of the QTSQ
tensor format, nor any future hosted, cloud, enterprise, or managed
offerings. Those remain proprietary — see `LICENSES/QTSQ-FORMAT.txt` for
the QTSQ format terms. Note: that license grants free use of the Format
through Sofuu itself (personal and commercial, no fees); what stays
restricted is forking the spec and independent competing implementations.
The full boundary is documented in `docs/OPEN-CORE.md`.
